IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `aa-awards`

-- Arbitration Act 2001, ss 3, 4, 6, 12-15, 20, 21, 38, 39, 43, 46, 48-50 and 59 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_arbitration-act-2001.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`an oral deal later minuted` MEANS `Agreement facts` WITH
    `content recorded in any form` IS TRUE
    `in an electronic communication accessible for later reference` IS FALSE
    `incorporated by a reference making the clause part of the contract` IS FALSE
    `asserted in a pleading calling for a reply and not denied` IS FALSE

`an email exchange kept on file` MEANS `Agreement facts` WITH
    `content recorded in any form` IS FALSE
    `in an electronic communication accessible for later reference` IS TRUE
    `incorporated by a reference making the clause part of the contract` IS FALSE
    `asserted in a pleading calling for a reply and not denied` IS FALSE

`a bill of lading incorporating a charterparty clause` MEANS `Agreement facts` WITH
    `content recorded in any form` IS FALSE
    `in an electronic communication accessible for later reference` IS FALSE
    `incorporated by a reference making the clause part of the contract` IS TRUE
    `asserted in a pleading calling for a reply and not denied` IS FALSE

`an unanswered pleading assertion` MEANS `Agreement facts` WITH
    `content recorded in any form` IS FALSE
    `in an electronic communication accessible for later reference` IS FALSE
    `incorporated by a reference making the clause part of the contract` IS FALSE
    `asserted in a pleading calling for a reply and not denied` IS TRUE

`a handshake with nothing recorded` MEANS `Agreement facts` WITH
    `content recorded in any form` IS FALSE
    `in an electronic communication accessible for later reference` IS FALSE
    `incorporated by a reference making the clause part of the contract` IS FALSE
    `asserted in a pleading calling for a reply and not denied` IS FALSE

`an obviously wrong decision` MEANS `Permission facts` WITH
    `substantially affects the rights of a party` IS TRUE
    `the tribunal was asked to determine it` IS TRUE
    `the decision is obviously wrong` IS TRUE
    `of general public importance` IS FALSE
    `at least open to serious doubt` IS FALSE
    `just and proper for the Court to decide` IS TRUE

`a doubtful decision of public importance` MEANS `Permission facts` WITH
    `substantially affects the rights of a party` IS TRUE
    `the tribunal was asked to determine it` IS TRUE
    `the decision is obviously wrong` IS FALSE
    `of general public importance` IS TRUE
    `at least open to serious doubt` IS TRUE
    `just and proper for the Court to decide` IS TRUE

`a doubtful decision of only private importance` MEANS `Permission facts` WITH
    `substantially affects the rights of a party` IS TRUE
    `the tribunal was asked to determine it` IS TRUE
    `the decision is obviously wrong` IS FALSE
    `of general public importance` IS FALSE
    `at least open to serious doubt` IS TRUE
    `just and proper for the Court to decide` IS TRUE

`a point never put to the tribunal` MEANS `Permission facts` WITH
    `substantially affects the rights of a party` IS TRUE
    `the tribunal was asked to determine it` IS FALSE
    `the decision is obviously wrong` IS TRUE
    `of general public importance` IS FALSE
    `at least open to serious doubt` IS FALSE
    `just and proper for the Court to decide` IS TRUE

`a wrong decision that changes nothing` MEANS `Permission facts` WITH
    `substantially affects the rights of a party` IS FALSE
    `the tribunal was asked to determine it` IS TRUE
    `the decision is obviously wrong` IS TRUE
    `of general public importance` IS FALSE
    `at least open to serious doubt` IS FALSE
    `just and proper for the Court to decide` IS TRUE

